{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Orbiting Panning and Zooming in Blender.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Orbiting Panning and Zooming in Blender.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"orbiting panning and zooming in blender orbiting panning and zooming in blender","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Orbiting Panning and Zooming in Blender.md","fileName":"Orbiting Panning and Zooming in Blender.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Orbiting Panning and Zooming in Blender","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-07 23:25\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Blender 3D Viewport and Object Operations]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Blender 3D Viewport and Object Operations","blenderfordummies4thedition.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Orbiting Panning and Zooming in Blender.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Orbiting Panning and Zooming in Blender.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"orbiting panning and zooming in blender orbiting panning and zooming in blender","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Orbiting Panning and Zooming in Blender.md","fileName":"Orbiting Panning and Zooming in Blender.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Orbiting Panning and Zooming in Blender","heading":"Orbiting Panning and Zooming in Blender","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"The 3D Viewport is a two-dimensional window onto a three-dimensional scene. Orbiting rotates the apparent world around a fixed point, panning shifts the view laterally, and zooming changes how much of the scene is visible.\n\nThinking of the scene as moving in front of the viewer clarifies these controls. Navigation changes the point of view, not the scene objects themselves, so it can be used freely while modeling or inspecting spatial relationships.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Blender 3D Viewport and Object Operatio